meta {
  name: Invitations - Create
  type: http
  seq: 67
}

post {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/communities/nswswk8w8wso0ko8owwk8k0w/invitations
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "grace@example.com",
    "role": "member",
    "access_groups": ["clx8ag0000000paid000000"],
    "member_tags": ["clx8mt0000000found00000"]
  }
}

docs {
  Invites an email address with a role lower than the role of the caller, and sends the invitation email (#1242). The signed link of the email works for 7 days, for an account with this email address only. Inviting the same address again replaces its invitation when the caller may give the role of that invitation (403 otherwise; an expired invitation is replaced by any manager). A member of the community gives a validation issue. A personal community invites nobody (422). Optional access_groups and member_tags (#1390): cuids of groups and tags of the community (at most 50 and 20, a duplicate counts once; at most 100 and 40 items as they come in) that the person gets when they accept the invitation; a cuid of another community is a validation issue on its field. Groups need the right to manage the members of access groups and, for a token, groups:write; tags need the right to assign member tags and, for a token, member-tags:write (403 otherwise). An empty list needs nothing. The new invitation of an address has the lists of the new request only. Rate limited (10 per minute).
}
